Requested per CARRYOVER.md section A item 4, to find when svc-entraconnect's password actually
expires. It was created with PasswordNeverExpires: False (Raymond's deliberate deviation from
the given command), so it's subject to the domain's default password policy rather than exempt
from it.

Command: Get-ADDefaultDomainPasswordPolicy | Select MaxPasswordAge
Host: DC01 (VM 100), via qm guest exec from Proxmox host
Timestamp: 2026-09-01 (UTC, exact time not recorded)

{
   "exitcode" : 0,
   "exited" : 1,
   "out-data" : "\r\nMaxPasswordAge\r\n--------------\r\n42.00:00:00   \r\n\r\n\r\n"
}

svc-entraconnect's PasswordLastSet was already captured this exercise, in
evidence/svc-entraconnect-account-state.json: 9/1/2026 7:54:57 AM.

RESULT: MaxPasswordAge is 42 days. PasswordLastSet (9/1/2026 7:54:57 AM) plus 42 days puts
svc-entraconnect's password expiry at approximately 2026-10-13, ~07:54 local. If nothing
rotates it before then, Entra Connect sync will start failing on connector account
authentication around that date, likely surfacing as import/export errors in Synchronization
Service Manager rather than an obvious "password expired" message. Worth a calendar reminder or
a fine-grained password policy exemption before that date, whichever Raymond prefers — not
acted on here, informational only.
